  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Quiet weather period with warming trend this week.\n\n\nRemaining clouds across the area have started to dissipate\nduring the overnight period. This is due to surface high\npressure settling into the region across the area from the Ohio\nvalley. This surface high pressure system will remain fixed\nacross the region through much of the week ahead, and lead to\npredominantly dry conditions areawide, with no precipitation\nforecast through Friday of this week. \n\n500mb heights will gradually increase throughout the week, \nwhich will inevitably lead to warmer 850mb temperatures across \nthe region. These increased 850mb temperatures will allow \ntemperatures to moderate back to near normal temperatures \nthrough the middle of the work week, and above normal \ntemperatures by the end of the work week. Highs today will \ngenerally be near average or slightly below average in the \n40s/50s across the area, with widespread 60s to near 70 \novertaking the area by midweek. While daytime highs will warm up\nto these temperatures, clear skies and calm winds will allow \nfor efficient radiational cooling each night with some lows in \nthe 20s and gradually \"warming\" into the 30s.",
